From: SBE1V1K build <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommbe: sbe1v1k: carry over the 24.10 boot blockers

v24 刷进路由器 B 后链路有 carrier 但 LAN 零流量、拿不到 DHCP，系统没有
起到用户态。对比 24.10-6.6 的真机结论，25.12 的设备树缺了三处已经在
同一块板子上被证明为启动阻塞的写法（24.10 的
build/p-b/files/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574-sbe1v1k.dts 是基线）：

1. CPU OPP 表。ipq9574.dtsi 给四个 CPU 都挂 operating-points-v2；
   qualcommbe 的 config-6.12 打开 CONFIG_CPUFREQ_DT、
   CONFIG_CPUFREQ_DT_PLATDEV（cpufreq-dt-platdev.c 里有
   "qcom,ipq9574"）与 CONFIG_ARM_QCOM_CPUFREQ_NVMEM，于是 cpufreq-dt
   在 OPP 表可用时就会注册。它第一次 dev_pm_opp_set_rate() 重写 APCS
   mux 和 A73 PLL，板子在用户态之前静默死亡。24.10 同一颗芯片上：
   v52/v53/v54（cpufreq 上线）都没到用户态，v50（cpufreq 注册失败）和
   v55（OPP 表不存在）都起来了。两个内核都没有这些核的电压管理
   （没有 CPR/APM），本来也没有安全的调频可做。

2. sleep_clk 的 32 kHz 速率。ipq9574-rdp-common.dtsi 给它赋了
   clock-frequency；24.10 的记录是“每个起不来的 DTB 都有这个速率”，
   出厂可用 DTS 故意不写。它唯一的消费者是 qcom_wdt，删掉后看门狗停在
   deferred probe，系统照常启动（24.10 v55，2026-11-13）。

3. nss@40000000 的 32 MiB 保留区（0x40000000..0x42000000，厂商内存图，
   S1/S2 都有）。mainline ipq9574.dtsi 不保留它，内核分配器会把这 32 MiB
   发出去；0024 用的 0x42200000 装载地址正好紧挨着它。

DHCP 与 WiFi 的相关性尚未在真机上区分，因此这里只搬 24.10 已被硬件
证明的启动条件，不引入新机制。DTB 已用 dtc 编译并反编译核对：cpus 下
没有 operating-points-v2，sleep-clk 没有 clock-frequency，
reserved-memory 含 nss@40000000。CI 在 prepare-tree（源码断言）与
verify-image（反编译编出的 DTB）两处检查。

Status: static only, NOT TESTED on hardware.
---
--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/files/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574-sbe1v1k.dts
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/files/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574-sbe1v1k.dts
@@ -654,3 +654,54 @@
 		     <0 334 4>,		/* PPEDS 3 Rx desc */
 		     <0 358 4>;		/* PPEDS 3 Rx fill */
 };
+/*
+ * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ * Boot blockers carried over from the hardware-proven 24.10-6.6 board tree
+ * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ */
+
+/*
+ * Disable cpufreq on this board.
+ *
+ * ipq9574.dtsi gives all four CPUs an operating-points-v2 table, and the
+ * qualcommbe target turns on CONFIG_CPUFREQ_DT, CONFIG_CPUFREQ_DT_PLATDEV
+ * (cpufreq-dt-platdev.c matches "qcom,ipq9574") and
+ * CONFIG_ARM_QCOM_CPUFREQ_NVMEM, so cpufreq-dt registers as soon as the OPP
+ * table resolves.  Its first dev_pm_opp_set_rate() reprograms the APCS mux
+ * and the A73 PLL and the board dies silently before userland.  The same
+ * silicon produced exactly that on 24.10-6.6: v52/v53/v54 (cpufreq online)
+ * never reached userland, while v50 (cpufreq could not register at all) and
+ * v55 (OPP table absent) both did.  Neither kernel has voltage management
+ * for these cores (no CPR/APM), so there is no safe transition to offer
+ * anyway; APPSBL already left the CPUs at a usable rate.  Every 25.12 image
+ * up to v24 still carried the table and never booted.
+ */
+&CPU0 { /delete-property/ operating-points-v2; };
+&CPU1 { /delete-property/ operating-points-v2; };
+&CPU2 { /delete-property/ operating-points-v2; };
+&CPU3 { /delete-property/ operating-points-v2; };
+
+/*
+ * Drop the 32 kHz sleep clock rate that ipq9574-rdp-common.dtsi assigns.  In
+ * the 24.10 board tree a sleep_clk rate was present in every DTB that failed
+ * to boot, and the shipping DTS deliberately leaves the property out.  Its
+ * only consumer here is the qcom_wdt watchdog at 0xb017000, which then stays
+ * in deferred probe; the system boots and runs without it (24.10 v55,
+ * 2026-11-13).  Revisit the watchdog as its own item.
+ */
+&sleep_clk { /delete-property/ clock-frequency; };
+
+/*
+ * The NSS firmware window of the vendor memory map: 32 MiB at
+ * 0x40000000..0x42000000, carried by both vendor device trees (S1 and S2)
+ * and reserved by the 24.10 board tree.  mainline ipq9574.dtsi does not
+ * reserve it, so the kernel allocator would otherwise hand the region out;
+ * the 0x42200000 kernel load address (patch 0024) sits right behind it.
+ */
+&{/reserved-memory} {
+	nss@40000000 {
+		no-map;
+		reg = <0x0 0x40000000 0x0 0x2000000>;
+		status = "okay";
+	};
+};
